KG42.register("rules-04627eceb20d683f83694c16",{"id":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization::v141-c-R004","paper":"21-dso_flexibility_optimization","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R004","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M01","name":"Local market coordinator","process_stage":"coordination","market_meaning":"The SESP, acting as aggregator, receives DSO flexibility requests specifying minimum active-energy variations relative to the forecast baseline, without knowing grid-status information. Scope: DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. The SESP's coordination of corrective actions must give DSO needs maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads. Scope: SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. Condition: During a DSO-designated yellow-light grid situation. The SESP may send direct control signals overriding local household energy-management decisions. Scope: SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. Condition: During a grid-constrained yellow-light situation. The SESP's forecast must have DSO approval before it is used as the baseline scenario. Scope: Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline. Condition: When a consumption or generation forecast for a flexible asset is to be used as the baseline scenario.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function coordination.local_operator under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R004-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"coordination.local_operator","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g02-ev33"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"coordination","context_text":"DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market. | SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. | SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. | Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g01-ev-004","v141-b-g01-ev-011","v141-b-g01-ev-014","v141-b-g02-ev33"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP, acting as aggregator, receives DSO flexibility requests specifying minimum active-energy variations relative to the forecast baseline, without knowing grid-status information. Scope: DSO upward- and downward-regulation requests in the SESP-operated local flexibility market.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-001","v141-b-g01-ev-003","v141-b-g02-ev33"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP's coordination of corrective actions must give DSO needs maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads. Scope: SESP coordination of corrective actions in the local flexibility market. Condition: During a DSO-designated yellow-light grid situation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-004"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP may send direct control signals overriding local household energy-management decisions. Scope: SESP control authority over local household resource decisions. Condition: During a grid-constrained yellow-light situation.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-014"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The SESP's forecast must have DSO approval before it is used as the baseline scenario. Scope: Use of SESP forecasts as the flexibility-market baseline. Condition: When a consumption or generation forecast for a flexible asset is to be used as the baseline scenario.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-ev-011"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-001","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p03-c2r4__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"be In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for or sending information, t","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"A local flexibility market (LFM) is an electricity trading platform to sell and buy flexibility in geographically limited areas like neighbourhoods and small towns. The SESP is the local market platform provider and community aggregator (AGR). At the same time, the SESP is a BRP from the regulatory point of view because it bids in wholesale markets. In order to run these markets, local traders need the SESP Platform for sending information, trading for flexibility, and scheduling actions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-003","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p02-c2r4__v141-a-M01-coordination","page":2,"printed_page":"882","section":"2.1. Centralized local flexibility market approaches","anchor_text":"on same distribution transformer have to be members of the same BRP and diﬀerent BRP could not be in","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-02.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"In contrast  in  this work, AGR receives DSO requests without knowing grid status information to solve grid congestion problems in the daily basis. In order to attend its demands, AGR controls flexible assets using a market-based methodology."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-004","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p03-c2r2__v141-a-M01-participation","page":3,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"[ ] w In contrast to the previous studied works, this paper presents a te novel and innovative propo","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-03.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Furthermore and according to the Traffic Light Concept (TLC) proposed by the German Association of Energy and Water (BDEW) [44] and the study by Zoeller et al. [45], the present problem formulation is designed for situations where the DSO determined a yellow light situation in a grid zone and it wants to go back to the green light status. Thereafter, the DSO asks the SESP to apply corrective actions in exchange for economic compensation previously established on their contract. During yellow light situations, the DSO needs have maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads and prosumers or ARG priorities are not considered."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-011","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p05-c1r2__v141-a-M01-activation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"Fig. 4. System des 1. The consumption or generation forecast of every ﬂexible asset is re done by th","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"1. The consumption or generation forecast of every flexible asset is done by the SESP and it needs the approval of the DSO to be used as the base line scenario.\n2. Once the SESP sends a command to a flexible resource in order to modify its generation/consumption, the amount of the activated flexibility is counted as the absolute value of the difference between the predicted power consumption/generation and the measured power in the device metering point.\n3. The activation of the flexibility ends when the SESP sends an END command permitting the resource to operate freely again."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-014","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M01-activation","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":null,"anchor_text":"ge LC are small computers with communication capabilities for rehouseholds to monitor and control pr","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Local controllers can take decisions during non-constrained situations about the energy management of the household resources. Nevertheless, during grid constrained situations like yellow and red light, the SESP and the DSO can send direct control signals respectively avoiding the local decisions."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev33","location":{"location_id":"src-58f2111926-p08-c2r2__v141-a-M01-pricing","page":8,"printed_page":"888","section":"4.5. DSO request constraints","anchor_text":", nd Tkend,c − (V kend,c − Vkstart,c ) me ρk ,c = ∑ γk ,t · t ∀ k ∈ K SP ,∀ c ∈ C (k ) t = Tkstart,c","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Finally, DSO constraints represent the request for fulﬁlling upward and downward regulation. These constraints are deﬁned as the minimum required amount of active energy variation with respect to the forecasted baseline scenario and are denoted as DtDSO. Positives and negative values of DtDSO mean upward and downward regulation re-spectively."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"The frozen rule defines no design-selection or operational decision variable. Its constraints govern the SESP coordinator's information, priority, direct-control and approval conditions, not a quantity selected by an optimization in this rule's scope.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed numeric or symbolic parameter is declared for the frozen procedural constraints. The DSO request D_t^DSO and the clearing-model parameters and variables appear in the clearing rule R003 and are not reused here without explicit graph support in R004."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M01-activation","v141-a-M01-bidding","v141-a-M01-clearing","v141-a-M01-coordination","v141-a-M01-participation","v141-a-M01-settlement"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"coordination.local_operator","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-003","quote":"AGR receives DSO requests without knowing grid status information to solve grid congestion problems in the daily basis."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-001","quote":"The SESP is the local market platform provider and community aggregator (AGR)."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-ev33","quote":"Finally, DSO constraints represent the request for fulﬁlling upward and downward regulation. These constraints are deﬁned as the minimum required amount of active energy variation with respect to the forecasted baseline scenario and are denoted as DtDSO."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-004","quote":"Thereafter, the DSO asks the SESP to apply corrective actions in exchange for economic compensation previously established on their contract. During yellow light situations, the DSO needs have maximum priority to avoid over-voltages or transformer over-loads and prosumers or ARG priorities are not considered."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-014","quote":"Nevertheless, during grid constrained situations like yellow and red light, the SESP and the DSO can send direct control signals respectively avoiding the local decisions."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-ev-011","quote":"The consumption or generation forecast of every flexible asset is done by the SESP and it needs the approval of the DSO to be used as the base line scenario."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"e968f0d45db770f14a0c8c563237c8977ffb1e7fb5e2e9eeee989bd1f3b4633a","applicability":"non_mathematical","reason":"The four frozen constraints for this coordination rule are procedural: the SESP receives DSO flexibility requests without grid-status information, gives DSO needs maximum priority during a yellow-light situation, may send direct control signals overriding local household decisions during grid-constrained situations, and must obtain DSO approval before using an SESP forecast as the baseline scenario. The supplied B evidence states institutional permissions, priorities and approvals rather than an algebraic relation in this rule's scope. The related mathematical DSO-request inequalities and resource variables belong to the clearing rule R003 and cannot be moved or reused here under the frozen V/E. Therefore this rule is treated as non_mathematical with no x or theta objects.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C001","node_ids":["bidding.demand","coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R004-E001"],"rationale":"C001 describes DSO demand requests received by the SESP coordinator. The frozen edge E001 links bidding.demand to coordination.local_operator, matching the stated request-receipt relation. The constraint is procedural and not given an algebraic expression in this rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C002","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C002 governs the priority assigned by the SESP coordinator during a yellow-light situation. It does not add a separate demand or clearing object in the frozen R004 graph."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C003","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C003 governs the SESP coordinator's direct-control authority over local household decisions during grid-constrained situations. The frozen R004 graph contains only the coordinator node for this authority and no household-decision node."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R004-C004","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"C004 imposes a DSO-approval condition on use of SESP forecasts as the market baseline. The frozen R004 graph has no separate forecast or baseline node, so the constraint is attached only to the coordinating operator."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
